  "evidence_policy": "Four positive full-field SvcScan multiset cases. Empty SvcDiff cases do not enter positive evidence. SvcList reruns do not double-count existing cases. No full plugin contract claimed.",
  "known_limitations": [
    "Only explicitly mapped Intel x86/x64 service layouts; no ARM64 support. SvcList/SvcDiff require Win10 15063+ x64.",
    "Standard SvcScan has eleven fields; legacy windows.svcscan remains a separate eight-column contract.",
    "No PID option, matching pinned reference. Scan scope is all services.exe VADs, capped at 128 MiB per process and 65536 records per chain.",
    "Missing pages, cycles, invalid registry siblings and invalid records retain partial diagnostics and cannot enter successful caches.",
    "For serH tuples, fresh runtime absent values prevent reference deduplication; shared precomputed registry absences can compare equal. Full multiset verification preserves exact multiplicity.",
    "NT5 direct sErv scan has synthetic boundary tests and Server2003 x86 native regression, but pinned reference rejects this build. NT5 differential parity remains unverified.",
    "SvcDiff matches service names case-sensitively and keeps the last scan occurrence. Two actual empty cases are negative agreement only, not hidden-service detection proof.",
    "No real malicious hidden-service or intentionally cyclic-list image validated. Hive pool fallback and other SvcList limitations remain; see svclist-known-limitations.json.",
    "Coverage applies only to the exact recorded builds and images, not every build in a compatibility target."
  ],
  "synthetic_tests": [
    "modern header alignment, full-tuple deduplication and fresh/shared absent-value semantics",
    "NT5 direct tags crossing pages, missing-page carry reset",
    "name-based differences, exact case, last occurrence per name",
    "unrelated unreadable data and invalid registry value nodes do not hide later target; partial diagnostics retained",
    "multiset comparison rejects differing counts, field values and one-sided absence; default duplicate rejection unchanged"
  ]
}
